// # 2026-09-10 — install/ Focused Audit
//
// Logline: install/ is clean against RULES §1.14 (file law), §1.8 (256-line
//          cap), §1.11 (4-element header), and §1.24 (VERSION SSoT). One
//          real drift remains: the harness count is reported as 5 different
//          numbers across 4 files (20 / 18 / 15 / 12 / 10), so the contract
//          between the curl|bash path and the cap-closed .oo path is fuzzy.
//
// Setup: Pin v0.1.30-9-g0795f78 (HEAD 0795f78 2026-09-10 08:22 +1000,
//        tag v0.1.30, VERSION 0.1.30, INDEX.oot:36 says v0.1.30 — all
//        clean). Read with install/ANCHOR.oo, install/harness_wire.oo,
//        install/install.sh (1426 lines, .sh carve-out RULES §1.14),
//        and openOODA/RULES.oot §1.14 amendment 2026-09-10.
//        Prior 2026-09-10 mcp-lsp-blackbox-usability audit (untracked,
//        audit/2026-09-10-mcp-lsp-blackbox-usability.oot) already closed
//        28 wire-function bugs; this audit covers the install/ repo only.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Severity summary.
//   2. M1: 5-way harness count drift.
//   3. M2: install.sh hybrid path is documented in README only, not in ANCHOR.oo.
//   4. M3: install.sh trusts .oo for 10 harnesses; .oo only wires 8 of them.
//   5. m1-m3: minor drift (changelog, README line count, no qa/ dir).
//   6. N1-N5: governance compliance (all PASS).
//   7. Out-of-lane (none — install/ has no cross-repo handoffs this audit).

// 1. SEVERITY SUMMARY --------------------------------------------------
//
// | Sev      | Count | Findings                                          |
// |----------|-------|---------------------------------------------------|
// | CRITICAL | 0     | (none)                                            |
// | MAJOR    | 3     | M1 (5-way count drift), M2 (hybrid undocumented), |
// |          |       | M3 (.oo trust-list 2 too wide)                    |
// | MINOR    | 3     | m1 (changelog 0.1.0), m2 (no qa/), m3 (README 172) |
// | NOTE     | 5     | N1 (4-element header), N2 (file law),             |
// |          |       | N3 (256-line cap), N4 (VERSION), N5 (detect=20)   |
//
// 2. M1: 5-WAY HARNESS COUNT DRIFT ------------------------------------
//
// One concept ("how many harnesses does install wire?") has 5 different
// numbers in 4 files. This is the contract gap.
//
// | Source                                  | Count | What it covers                       |
// |-----------------------------------------|-------|--------------------------------------|
// | install/ANCHOR.oo:11 Beat 3             |  20   | detect list (matches install.sh)     |
// | install/install.sh detect_harnesses()   |  20   | antigravity-cli, opencode, muse,     |
// |   (lines 511-532)                       |       | grok, gemini, claude-code,            |
// |                                         |       | claude-desktop, cursor, windsurf,    |
// |                                         |       | codex, cline, continue, zed, vscode,  |
// |                                         |       | goose, mistral-vibe, grok-build,     |
// |                                         |       | devin, charm, mcode                  |
// | install/install.sh wire_* funcs         |  18   | all of above MINUS devin, charm      |
// |   (lines 543-1115)                      |       | (detected, never wired)              |
// | install/harness_wire.oo:3 Logline       |  15   | "15 LLM harnesses" (WRONG — 12 wire) |
// | install/harness_wire.oo actual          |  12   | opencode, gemini, cursor, zed,       |
// |   (12 wire funcs, lines 76-184 + main)  |       | claude-desktop, windsurf, vscode,    |
// |                                         |       | continue (8 file), plus agy, vibe,   |
// |                                         |       | codex, claude (4 ProcessCap stubs)   |
// | install/install.sh:1144 case list       |  10   | trusts .oo for: opencode, gemini,   |
// |   (.oo-wired assumption)                |       | cursor, windsurf, zed, vscode,       |
// |                                         |       | goose, claude-desktop, cline,        |
// |                                         |       | continue — see M3                     |
//
// Truth:
//   detect = 20 (install.sh is the only canonical source)
//   wire   = 18 in bash + 12 in .oo (overlapping, not additive)
//   The "20" claim in ANCHOR.oo Beat 3 is the detect list, not the wire list.
//
// Root cause: the 4 documents (ANCHOR.oo, harness_wire.oo Logline, .oo
// reality, install.sh case) were written at different times during the
// 2026-09-10 hybrid migration (commits 53e6cee → d737843 → ccc13ed → 4a03bf4).
// Each was locally correct at the time but the consolidation was never
// made canonical.
//
// Fix: ANCHOR.oo Beat 3 should say "detects 20, wires 18 in bash + 12 in
// .oo (8 file + 4 ProcessCap stubs); devin and charm are detected but
// not yet wired." harness_wire.oo Logline should drop "15" in favor of
// "12 (8 file merges + 4 ProcessCap CLI stubs)". This is a doc-only fix.

// 3. M2: HYBRID PATH DOCUMENTED IN README, NOT IN ANCHOR.oo -----------
//
// install.sh:1133-1156 implements a "harness_wire.oo tried first, bash
// merges as fallback" hybrid. The fallback fires when (a) ooda+oodac
// are not installed (curl|bash default), (b) harness_wire.oo is not on
// disk, or (c) `ooda run harness_wire.oo` fails. install.sh:1149 logs
// "harness_wire.oo failed — fallback to bash".
//
// README.md:40 documents the hybrid:
//   cap-closed `harness_wire.oo` (172 lines) tried first (silent unless
//   `OPENOODA_DEBUG=1`, falls back to bash for `curl | bash`).
//
// But install/ANCHOR.oo Beat 5 says only:
//   "No python fallback in .oo path."
//
// The Beat is technically true (the .oo file has no python), but the
// install.sh bash path has 20+ python3 heredoc invocations (lines 563,
// 605, 675, 698, 737, 771, 791, 812, 837, 865, 940, 965, 989, 1015, 1040,
// 1097) and is the only path that runs at first install. So a reader of
// ANCHOR.oo alone concludes "no python anywhere" and is wrong.
//
// Fix: add Beat 6 to ANCHOR.oo: "Hybrid wiring: install.sh runs bash
// + python3 heredoc merges for 18 harnesses (default, curl|bash path).
// If ooda+oodac are on PATH, install.sh also runs harness_wire.oo for
// 12 of them; on failure, falls back to bash. OPENOODA_DEBUG=1 enables
// .oo-path logging."

// 4. M3: install.sh TRUST LIST OVER-CLAIMS .oo COVERAGE BY 2 ---------
//
// install.sh:1144 case statement marks these 10 as wired-by-.oo when
// `ooda run harness_wire.oo` returns 0:
//
//   opencode, gemini, cursor, windsurf, zed, vscode,
//   goose, claude-desktop, cline, continue
//
// harness_wire.oo actually wires only 8 of these via file merge:
//   opencode (line 103), gemini (119), cursor (127), zed (135),
//   claude-desktop (inline c1 at line 203), windsurf (inline c2 at 205),
//   vscode (inline c3 at 207), continue (inline c4 at 209).
//
// goose and cline are NOT wired by harness_wire.oo — there is no
// wire_goose or wire_cline function in the file. But because install.sh
// adds them to HARNESS_WIRED and the bash fallback at line 1157-1158
// skips them ("already wired"), the user gets silent no-ops for
// goose and cline on the .oo path.
//
// Reproduction path:
//   1. install ooda + oodac to ~/.openooda/bin/.
//   2. install goose and cline to their well-known paths.
//   3. set OPENOODA_DEBUG=1; run install.sh.
//   4. oodac harness_wire.oo → returns 0 (12 funcs).
//   5. install.sh:1144 marks goose, cline as wired.
//   6. install.sh:1157 case statement skips bash wire.
//   7. Result: ~/.config/goose/config.yaml + ~/.config/Code/.../cline_*
//      are NOT actually wired. Silent.
//
// Fix: trim install.sh:1144 case list to the 8 the .oo actually wires:
//   opencode|gemini|cursor|windsurf|zed|vscode|claude-desktop|continue
// And the corresponding skip list at install.sh:1157-1158.
//
// Alternative: add wire_goose + wire_cline to harness_wire.oo and bring
// the .oo count to 14. That's the cleaner long-term fix but adds ~40
// lines (still under 256-line cap, with current 214 + 42 = 256). This
// audit recommends the trim — it's smaller and matches the truth.

// 5. MINOR DRIFT ------------------------------------------------------
//
// m1. install/apt/debian/changelog:1 says `openooda (0.1.0-1) unstable`
//     while VERSION:1 is `0.1.30`. The debian changelog is stale by
//     0.1.30 versions. Not user-facing (debian/ is shipped via apt/
//     Makefile, not as a release), but the drift is real. Fix: bump
//     to `0.1.30-1 unstable` (debian policy: only the maintainer
//     cuts a new upstream release; 0.1.30-1 is a packaging-only bump).
//
// m2. install/ has 0 qa/ files. The qa/ convention is `qa-NN-name.oo`
//     with `qa/ANCHOR.oo`. Sibling repos: blackbox/qa/ (25 + 1 ANCHOR),
//     lsp/qa/ (36), mcp/qa/ (19), opm/qa/ (18), catalog/qa/ (5),
//     ooda/qa/ (14). The user's 16:58 directive was "main qa is in
//     std, each repo how its own qa for repo specific stuff". tests/
//     (test_install.sh 80 lines, test_hello60.sh 65, test_hello60_inner.sh
//     56, hello_fixture.oo 13) is the install/ test surface but is not
//     in the qa/ naming convention. Fix would be `mkdir -p qa` +
//     `qa/ANCHOR.oo` + 1-2 `qa-NN-install_smoke.oo` probes. This is
//     new product code (per session invariant "process work, not new
//     product code") — flag, do not patch without user direction.
//
// m3. install/README.md:40 says `harness_wire.oo (172 lines)`. Actual
//     is 214 lines (line count: 214). Drift of 42 lines / 24%. Likely
//     from when the file had 172 lines (before 4a03bf4 "every server
//     env sets READDIR+WRITEDIR" added 6 env vars per wire function).
//     Fix: README.md:40 → `harness_wire.oo (214 lines)`.
//
// m4. install.sh:435 still mentions `ooda-mcp-grok|ooda-lsp-grok` in
//     a pgrep — these binaries never shipped (the grok shim was
//     removed by 0795f78 "grok shims, vibe env, gemini compiler,
//     mcode, codex fetch"). The grep is a kill-target for any leaked
//     process, not a producer, so it's a defensive belt-and-suspenders
//     that does no harm but never matches. Out of scope for this audit
//     (would need a behavioral run to verify the .oo path is now safe
//     without the pgrep); noted here for completeness.

